            {
                "entry_id": "625befa0-3c29-335d-8dea-01dc1885431a",
                "word": "Cameroon",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "ee58e868-0172-4253-bdb2-7a2c931b2c21",
                        "entry_id": "625befa0-3c29-335d-8dea-01dc1885431a",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "Cameroons"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9518e42a-6d95-3375-a4df-aecdbee2bb8f",
                        "entry_id": "625befa0-3c29-335d-8dea-01dc1885431a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A Conservative Party member with green or social liberal leanings, supporting the policies of David Cameron."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "78b16099-dece-4d5e-9f8d-a24e51fad996",
                                "sense_id": "9518e42a-6d95-3375-a4df-aecdbee2bb8f",
                                "text": "He fears that in downplaying traditional Conservative causes, in changing the party to be more in tune with modern Britain, the Cameroons have in effect accepted that they won't change the country much in office."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "610fcc5e-4c40-4f4c-a704-7285956fb0e8",
                                "sense_id": "9518e42a-6d95-3375-a4df-aecdbee2bb8f",
                                "text": "Today, I spy a coalition outrider: Nick Boles, MP for Grantham, founder of Policy Exchange and the archetypal Cameroon ultra-modernizer. I don’t think Boles even owned a tie until he was elected to the House of Commons. That’s how much of a Cameroon the man is."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "575bf7b4-1a07-4125-a190-a273d3d0fdd9",
                                "sense_id": "9518e42a-6d95-3375-a4df-aecdbee2bb8f",
                                "text": "Maude was a moderniser before modernity dawned in the Tory ranks, a Cameroon before David Cameron."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a969f417-14fe-4f54-9e76-d2692d9a2710",
                                "sense_id": "9518e42a-6d95-3375-a4df-aecdbee2bb8f",
                                "text": "Mr Cameron won significantly smaller vote shares than either Theresa May or Boris Johnson. There are not many Cameroons in Britain. Outside some newspaper op-ed pages, there never were."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
        ],
